# Template only — no real values. Copy to `.env.production.local` and fill in
# the actual production Neon connection string ONLY when you deliberately need
# a local script (e.g. a one-off admin script) to target production directly.
# This is the rare/explicit case, not the default — everyday `npm run dev` /
# `npm run seed` / etc. should keep using the dev branch via `.env` /
# `.env.development.local`.
#
# `.env.production.local` itself is gitignored (like all `.env*` files except
# this `.example`), so it never gets committed once you create it.
#
# To use it deliberately for a specific command:
#   npx tsx --env-file=.env.production.local some-script.ts
#
# DATABASE_URL is the only thing this file needs to override — all other vars
# (PAYLOAD_SECRET, HOSTINGER_*, NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL) fall through from `.env`
# unchanged.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<production-host>/<db>?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
